          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A step further"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.26,
            0.124,
            0.859,
            0.226
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Today, the lithium-ion (Li-ion) battery is the most common type of rechargeable battery, found in almost all devices that use batteries. These batteries rely on special metals like lithium and cobalt, which are mined and processed in limited parts of the world. Because of this, countries are now racing to secure supplies, recycle old batteries, and develop new technologies."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.081,
            0.22,
            0.248,
            0.337
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 2,
              "bbox": [
                0.081,
                0.22,
                0.248,
                0.337
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_12_image_2.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.26,
            0.226,
            0.86,
            0.33
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Scientists are also working on the next big leap: solid-state batteries, which replace the liquid or paste-like electrolytes with solid materials. These future batteries would be much safer, charge faster and last longer. Improved rechargeable batteries are very important as the world moves to developing environmentally friendly sources of electrical power."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.063,
            0.352,
            0.212,
            0.497
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 4,
              "bbox": [
                0.063,
                0.352,
                0.212,
                0.497
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_12_image_4.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.379,
            0.332,
            0.4
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Snapshots"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.22,
            0.418,
            0.866,
            0.471
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When electric current flows through a conductor (like a wire), it produces a magnetic field around it. This phenomenon is known as the magnetic effect of electric current."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.22,
            0.472,
            0.865,
            0.523
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A current carrying coil that behaves as a magnet is called an electromagnet. For practical applications, most electromagnets have an iron core to make them stronger."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.22,
            0.525,
            0.865,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Generation of heat in conductors due to flow of electric current is known as the heating effect of electric current."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.22,
            0.561,
            0.864,
            0.596
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A cell or a battery is a device that generates electric current because of chemical reactions taking place inside it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.22,
            0.597,
            0.857,
            0.616
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Rechargeable batteries can be recharged and reused multiple times."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.289,
            0.633,
